maria-support: FYI escalated from ACME — tool/function-calling keeps hitting 400 schema errors when the model returns, customer on Dedicated and blocked. They say call succeeds on OpenAI directly but fails through Redwood. See sample raw response below.

maria-support: Error we're seeing in their integration: `InvalidArgument: tool arguments must be a JSON object` and our validator complains about unexpected top-level wrapper. Customer pasted model output.

maria-support: Raw model payload (customer redacted ids):
```json
{
  "id": "resp_abc",
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "role": "tool",
        "name": "create_order",
        "tool_call": {
          "name": "create_order",
          "arguments": "{\"order_id\":\"12345\",\"currency\":\"USD\",\"amount\":\"100.00\"}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

maria-support: Note two things: (1) `arguments` is a JSON string not an object; (2) customer expects top-level fields (order_id, amount) but our schema validation expects `arguments` to be an object with `amount` as number and `currency` enum lowercased (usd|eur). They get `USD` which fails enum match.

jon-eng: I can take this. Likely cause: some model variants (or older OpenAI-compatible adapters) stringify args when prompts ask to "output JSON" or when tool calling is proxied. Also enum casing can differ depending on model.

jon-eng: Quick repro steps to run locally:
1) Use the same model the customer reported (they said `gpt-open-2025-small`) via our hosted endpoint.
2) Replay customer's conversation with `?debug=raw` to capture `choices[0].message.tool_call`.
3) Check `typeof arguments` and try `JSON.parse` if it's a string.

jon-eng: Suggested temporary mitigation for Support: add tolerant parsing in our validators for Dedicated customers: if `arguments` is a string, attempt `JSON.parse` and coerce enums to lowercase before strict validation. I'll propose a safe toggle so it isn't on by default.

maya-ml: Also confirm whether the customer is using the OpenAI "tool calling" format or a custom prompt that returns a wrapped object like `{ "result": {...} }`. If so, we should look for common wrappers and unwrap them. Short-term patch: accept either an object or a single-field wrapper and flatten if present.

maria-support: @jon-eng , customer provided their API request id: `req_0fX9` and Redwood trace id `trace-9987`. They attached a screenshot but raw JSON above is what they pasted. They want ETA — blocker for production.

jon-eng: Thanks. I'll start with logs: please pull `requests/req_0fX9/events` and include `model_raw_response` field. I need the full response headers and `model_version`. Can someone from infra paste the trace?

infra-bot: New internal ticket created: INF-4521 — "tool_call args stringified / enum casing mismatch". Linked traces: trace-9987, req_0fX9. SLA: P1 (customer Dedicated, production).

jon-eng: Patch plan: (a) add tolerant parser in request path that only runs for dedicated customers with a feature flag; (b) add normalizer to coerce enums (`toLowerCase()`) and numeric strings -> numbers for numeric params; (c) run canary for N customers. If accepted, I can PR today.

maya-ml: One extra thing — prompt-level guardrails: recommend customers include an explicit instruction to the model: `When using tool calling, set tool_call.arguments as a JSON object (not a string) and use lowercase for enum fields.` Provide them with a quick example.

maria-support: I'll send customer the workaround (try local parsing + prompt tweak) and ask for raw response capture. Can you own the fix, @jon-eng? Customer asked for ETA today.

jon-eng: I can own. ETA preliminary PR by EOD (demo tolerant parser + test cases), full rollout after canary 48h. Will ping here when PR is up.

maria-support: Thanks — I'll update ACME and attach ticket INF-4521. :thumbsup:

jon-eng: For reference, quick JS tolerant parse snippet I used during repro:
```js
function tolerantParseToolCall(tc) {
  let args = tc.arguments;
  if (typeof args === 'string') {
    try { args = JSON.parse(args); } catch (e) { return { error: 'arguments not parseable' }; }
  }
  // normalize enums -> lowercase keys/values as needed
  if (args.currency && typeof args.currency === 'string') args.currency = args.currency.toLowerCase();
  if (args.amount && typeof args.amount === 'string') args.amount = parseFloat(args.amount);
  return { name: tc.name, arguments: args };
}
```

maria-support: Attached to ticket and will follow up with ACME.

jon-eng: PR link when ready, I will include unit tests covering: stringified args, wrapped result object, enum casing, numeric-string coercion.

infra-bot: Reminder: if this fix touches validation layer used by Hosted customers, ensure feature flag default is OFF to avoid silent acceptance of malformed tool calls.

maria-support: End of thread — will reopen if ACME reports it still fails after workaround.
